---
// ROUND 05 — THE LIVE FRONTIER (the honest closer).
//
// The last beat of the engineer's evolution: not a win, the current edge. It
// names the live defect (the vocal goes tinny while the body stays full), the
// fix direction (protect the vocal, process the body, per track), the blind
// multi-rater roadmap, and wears "n=1 · not shipped" as a feature. The only
// number it will stand on is the -2 dBTP ceiling that survives streaming codecs.
//
// 100% server-rendered and visible with no JS (the honest readout must never
// hide behind a click). The ONLY script is a tiny class toggle on the defect
// glyph (defect <-> protected); no IntersectionObserver / scroll / rAF, so it
// survives the preview throttle. Rhymes with RoundFrame/TasteTrial (header,
// the-bet line, the verdict="live" yellow). Reduced-motion + keyboard safe.
---

<section class="lf" data-live-frontier>
  <header class="lf-head">
    <span class="lf-num">Round 05</span>
    <span class="lf-phase">the live frontier</span>
  </header>

  <p class="lf-belief">
    <span class="lf-belief-tag">the bet</span>
    This is where the engine actually is right now, not where it lands. Mastering the whole track at once, the vocal can go tinny while the body stays full. One curve cannot serve both. The next move is to protect the vocal and process the body on their own paths, surgically, per track. I have not shipped it. I am living the test.
  </p>

  <div class="lf-status">
    <span class="lf-stamp">n=1 · not shipped</span>
    <span class="lf-stamp-cap">One engine, one builder, living the test in the open. The honesty is the credibility: it is the opposite of a button that forgets you and overclaims.</span>
  </div>

  <!-- the defect: a neutral panel, because this is the problem, not the live edge -->
  <div class="lf-defect">
    <span class="lf-mini">the defect</span>
    <p class="lf-text">When it masters the whole track, the vocal can go thin and tinny while the body stays full and warm. A single processing curve cannot flatter both at the same time.</p>

    <div class="lf-glyph-wrap">
      <svg class="lf-glyph" viewBox="0 0 180 88" role="img" aria-hidden="true">
        <text x="2" y="27" class="lf-glyph-lab">vocal</text>
        <text x="2" y="70" class="lf-glyph-lab">body</text>
        <line x1="34" y1="44" x2="176" y2="44" class="lf-divider" />
        <!-- vocal: thin, brittle, spiking, thinning out at the right -->
        <rect class="lf-shield" x="33" y="11" width="140" height="30" rx="7" />
        <polyline class="lf-vocal" points="34,31 48,30 60,32 72,16 79,31 90,12 97,32 108,21 115,31 132,30 150,32 162,30" />
        <path class="lf-arrow" d="M168,17 L168,29 M164,25 L168,30 L172,25" />
        <!-- body: full, warm, rounded -->
        <path class="lf-body" d="M40,80 Q40,57 106,57 Q172,57 172,80 Z" />
      </svg>
      <span class="lf-sr">Two frequency bands. The vocal band on top is thin and spiking and thinning out. The body band below is full and rounded. The fix protects the vocal band and processes the body separately.</span>
      <button type="button" class="lf-glyph-toggle" data-lf-toggle aria-pressed="false">protect the vocal</button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- the fix: the live edge, accented yellow -->
  <div class="lf-fix">
    <span class="lf-mini">the fix</span>
    <p class="lf-text">Protect the vocal so it keeps its presence and never dries out. Process the body on its own path: clean it, shape it, give it room. Then meet the two cleanly. Per track, because every song wants a different balance.</p>
  </div>

  {/*
    FUTURE A/B HOOK — when Jon supplies two clips (vocal-saturated vs vocal-protected,
    same passage, loudness-matched), a <TheBench round={r5VocalAB} /> drops in here.
    Matches TheBench's BenchRound API:
      const r5VocalAB = {
        id: "r5-vocal", source: "<passage>", tag: "real audio · blind",
        loudnessNote: "Both matched to one loudness, so you judge the vocal, not the level.",
        takes: [
          { label: "the body processed, vocal untouched", file: `${REN}/r5-saturated.mp3` },
          { label: "the vocal protected, body processed", file: `${REN}/r5-protected.mp3` },
        ],
      };
    Ships invisible until then: no player chrome, no "coming soon".
  */}
  <div class="lf-bench-slot" data-audio-slot="round05-vocal-ab" hidden></div>

  <!-- the test: the blind multi-rater pipeline that ends in a ship-or-not gate -->
  <div class="lf-roadmap">
    <span class="lf-mini">the test</span>
    <div class="lf-pipe" role="list" aria-label="The blind test pipeline, in three stages">
      <div class="lf-stage" role="listitem">
        <span class="lf-stage-n">01</span>
        <span class="lf-stage-label">I crown blind</span>
      </div>
      <span class="lf-pipe-arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
      <div class="lf-stage" role="listitem">
        <span class="lf-stage-n">02</span>
        <span class="lf-stage-label">outsiders crown blind</span>
      </div>
      <span class="lf-pipe-arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
      <div class="lf-stage lf-stage-gate" role="listitem">
        <span class="lf-stage-n">03</span>
        <span class="lf-stage-label">re-score gate</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="lf-text">The method from here is one repeatable blind test. I crown blind first. Then listeners outside my own ear crown blind, loudness-matched, with no idea I built it, which strips the you-made-it bias I cannot strip from myself. From what both sets crown, I learn the per-track conditioning. Then the gate: it ships only if it beats doing nothing, blind, every single time.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- the floor: the one number, framed as a necessity cleared, not a victory -->
  <div class="lf-proof">
    <span class="lf-mini">the floor</span>
    <div class="lf-proof-row">
      <span class="lf-proof-num">&minus;2 dBTP</span>
      <p class="lf-text">The one number I will stand on: the true-peak ceiling is set to minus 2 dBTP. Lossy streaming codecs add inter-sample peaks when they re-encode, and a minus 1 dBTP master clips after the transcode. At minus 2 dBTP these masters survive it. That is the floor, cleared.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="lf-end">The aim is simple, and it is not finished yet: the master you prefer to doing nothing, proven blind.</p>
</section>

<script>
  // The only interactivity: flip the defect glyph to its protected state. Pure
  // class toggle on a server-rendered node, so no IO / scroll / rAF involved.
  const SR_DEFECT = "Two frequency bands. The vocal band on top is thin and spiking and thinning out. The body band below is full and rounded.";
  const SR_FIX = "Two frequency bands. The vocal band on top is now wrapped in a protective shield so it keeps its presence. The body band below is processed on its own path.";
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-lf-toggle]").forEach((btn) => {
    const defect = btn.closest(".lf-defect");
    const glyph = defect?.querySelector<SVGElement>(".lf-glyph");
    const sr = defect?.querySelector<HTMLElement>(".lf-sr");
    if (!glyph) return;
    btn.addEventListener("click", () => {
      const on = glyph.classList.toggle("is-fix");
      btn.setAttribute("aria-pressed", on ? "true" : "false");
      btn.textContent = on ? "show the defect" : "protect the vocal";
      // keep the screen-reader description in lockstep with the glyph state
      if (sr) sr.textContent = on ? SR_FIX : SR_DEFECT;
    });
  });
</script>

<style>
  .lf { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; color: #f5f1e8; }

  /* ── header + belief: rhyme RoundFrame / TasteTrial; only the num color shifts
        to yellow to signal the live frontier at a glance ── */
  .lf-head { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .lf-num {
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.24em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--brand-yellow);
  }
  .lf-phase {
    font-family: "Space Grotesk Variable", "Space Grotesk", ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-weight: 700; font-size: clamp(18px, 2.2vw, 22px); color: #f5f1e8; letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  .lf-belief {
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 13.5px; line-height: 1.6; color: rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.82);
    margin: 0 0 16px; max-width: 64ch;
  }
  .lf-belief-tag {
    display: inline-block; margin-right: 9px;
    font-size: 9px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.2em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.4); vertical-align: 1px;
  }

  /* ── the n=1 badge, worn high so honesty leads ── */
  .lf-status { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 14px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 18px; }
  .lf-stamp {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 10px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.18em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--brand-yellow); border: 1px solid currentColor; border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 4px 9px; white-space: nowrap; transform: rotate(-3deg);
  }
  .lf-stamp-cap {
    flex: 1 1 280px; min-width: 0;
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 11.5px; line-height: 1.5; color: rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.55);
  }

  /* ── shared panel chrome ── */
  .lf-defect, .lf-fix, .lf-roadmap, .lf-proof {
    background: rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.02);
    border: 1px solid var(--cs-line, rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.1));
    border-radius: 8px; padding: 14px 16px; margin-top: 12px;
  }
  .lf-defect { border-left: 2px solid rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.22); }
  .lf-fix { border-left: 2px solid var(--brand-yellow); }
  .lf-proof { border-left: 2px solid var(--brand-yellow); }
  .lf-roadmap { border-left: 2px solid rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.14); }
  .lf-mini {
    display: block; margin-bottom: 8px;
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 9px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.2em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.45);
  }
  .lf-text {
    margin: 0; max-width: 64ch;
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.62; color: var(--cs-text-muted, rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.7));
  }

  /* ── the defect glyph: vocal band thin/brittle, body band full ── */
  .lf-glyph-wrap { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; margin-top: 12px; }
  .lf-glyph { width: 200px; max-width: 100%; height: auto; }
  .lf-glyph-lab {
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 8px; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; fill: rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.5);
  }
  .lf-divider { stroke: rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.16); stroke-width: 1; }
  .lf-vocal { fill: none; stroke: #a06cf0; stroke-width: 1.6; stroke-linejoin: round; stroke-linecap: round; }
  .lf-body { fill: rgba(14, 196, 252, 0.18); stroke: #0ec4fc; stroke-width: 1.4; }
  .lf-arrow { fill: none; stroke: #a06cf0; stroke-width: 1.4; stroke-linecap: round; stroke-linejoin: round; transition: opacity 240ms ease; }
  .lf-shield { fill: none; stroke: var(--brand-yellow); stroke-width: 1; stroke-dasharray: 3 3; opacity: 0; transition: opacity 240ms ease; }
  .lf-glyph.is-fix .lf-arrow { opacity: 0; }
  .lf-glyph.is-fix .lf-shield { opacity: 0.9; }
  .lf-sr { position: absolute; width: 1px; height: 1px; padding: 0; margin: -1px; overflow: hidden; clip: rect(0, 0, 0, 0); white-space: nowrap; border: 0; }
  .lf-glyph-toggle {
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; font-size: 11px;
    color: rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.72); background: transparent;
    border: 1px solid rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.24); border-radius: 5px;
    padding: 6px 13px; cursor: pointer; transition: color 160ms ease, border-color 160ms ease, background 160ms ease;
  }
  .lf-glyph-toggle:hover { color: #f5f1e8; border-color: rgba(255, 179, 71, 0.5); background: rgba(255, 179, 71, 0.05); }
  .lf-glyph-toggle:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--brand-yellow); outline-offset: 2px; }
  .lf-glyph-toggle[aria-pressed="true"] { color: var(--brand-yellow); border-color: rgba(255, 179, 71, 0.5); }

  /* ── the blind-test pipeline ── */
  .lf-pipe { display: flex; align-items: stretch; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin: 4px 0 14px; }
  .lf-stage {
    flex: 1 1 0; min-width: 130px;
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 5px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.14); border-radius: 6px; padding: 10px 13px;
    background: rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.015);
  }
  .lf-stage-n {
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; font-size: 9px; font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em; color: rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.4);
  }
  .lf-stage-label {
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 1.35; color: #f5f1e8;
  }
  .lf-stage-gate {
    border-color: rgba(255, 179, 71, 0.5);
    background: rgba(255, 179, 71, 0.05);
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 22px -12px var(--brand-yellow);
  }
  .lf-stage-gate .lf-stage-n { color: var(--brand-yellow); }
  .lf-pipe-arrow { align-self: center; color: rgba(245, 241, 232, 0.32); font-size: 14px; flex: 0 0 auto; }

  /* ── the one number ── */
  .lf-proof-row { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .lf-proof-num {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    font-style: italic; font-weight: 700; font-size: 26px; letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    color: var(--brand-yellow); font-feature-settings: "tnum";
    text-shadow: 0 0 14px rgba(255, 179, 71, 0.3);
  }
  .lf-proof-row .lf-text { flex: 1 1 280px; }

  /* ── the aim ── */
  .lf-end {
    margin: 18px 0 0; max-width: 64ch;
    font-family: "Space Grotesk Variable", "Space Grotesk", ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: 16px; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.5; color: #f5f1e8;
  }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .lf-pipe { flex-direction: column; align-items: stretch; }
    .lf-pipe-arrow { transform: rotate(90deg); align-self: flex-start; margin-left: 14px; }
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .lf-arrow, .lf-shield, .lf-glyph-toggle { transition: none; }
  }
</style>
